course: dictionary
lesson: 3259
title: Equally: the same amount, just as much
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Equally is an adverb. It tells you how something is shared or how much something is the same. It has two main meanings: sharing so that everyone gets the same amount, and being just as much or just as good.
explain: «12 apples shared equally among 3 children» means each child gets the same number. 12 divided by 3 is 4, so each child gets 4 apples. The word tells you the share is fair, with no child getting more.
explain: Equally can also compare two things. «A feather and a hammer fall equally fast» means they fall at the same speed. A good check is to swap in the words «the same» or «just as» and see if the sentence still makes sense.
fact: Equally means so that everyone or every part gets the same amount.
fact: Equally can also mean just as much, to the same degree, as in «equally good».
fact: Equally is an adverb, so it can describe how something is done, as in «shared equally».
fact: «Treat everyone equally» means being fair to all people.
fact: A good check is to swap in «the same» or «just as»: «equally tall» means just as tall.
exercise: «12 apples shared equally among 3 children.» How many apples does each child get? | 12 | 3 | 9 | *4
exercise: «A feather and a hammer fall equally fast.» What does equally mean here? | Only one of them | Upside down | Very slowly | *At the same speed, just as fast
exercise: Which sentence uses equally to mean a fair share? | «The sun was very hot.» | «Dad drove the car home.» | *«Sam shared the sweets equally between his friends.» | «Mia had equally good ideas.»
test: «Treat everyone equally.» What does equally mean? | Only for the oldest people | *The same fair treatment for all | Quickly and without thinking | Without anyone knowing
test: Which word could replace equally in «equally tall»? | Slowly | Loudly | *Just as | Strangely
exam: Ravi says equally just means a lot. Is he right? | No, it means nobody gets anything | Yes, it means very quickly | Yes, it means a lot | *No, it means the same amount or just as much
